INT. MOVING VAN - CARGO BAY - DAY

Rain hammers the roof. A gray Tuesday smears past the rear windows.

CLOSE ON a laminated sign taped to a wardrobe box: "SYNERGY OFFSITE - DO NOT SHAKE."

HOLLIS
(checking a clipboard, not looking up)
Team, this relocation is a growth opportunity. Please buckle your milk crates.

PRIYA
(wedged between two filing cabinets, whispering)
Hollis, we're sitting on the furniture of a company that fired us this morning.

ANGLE ON the dashboard window behind the cab partition. The wipers beat like a slow pulse.

TOMASZ
(gripping the wheel, eyes on the mirror)
I'm just the driver. Nobody told me the passengers were also the cargo.

WE SEE a ceiling bulb swinging, throwing light across six tired faces.

WENDELL
(slowly peeling the tape off his own mouth)
I signed the NDA. I did not sign the van.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over the radio, crackling)
Unit Nine, confirm headcount. HR says there should be zero employees aboard.

INSERT - THE RADIO, its red light pulsing.

MARISOL
(standing, knocking over a lamp)
Zero? Hollis, what did you tell them about us?

HOLLIS
(clutching the clipboard to his chest)
I told them we were assets.

BACK TO SCENE

PRIYA
(shoving the cabinet, screaming)
Assets get depreciated!

TOMASZ
(slamming the brakes, everything crashing forward)
Everybody out! Now!
